			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Remove legacy PermissionManager module\n\nDelete the `Source/IPC/Security/PermissionManager.rs` file as part of the ongoing modularization and cleanup of the IPC security layer. This removal follows the recent pattern of decomposing monolithic IPC modules into fine-grained sub-files and enforcing strict PascalCase naming conventions.\n\nThe functionality previously housed in this file has either been migrated to dedicated sub-modules or is no longer required by the current `EnhancedIPC` architecture. This deletion reduces code clutter and aligns the security implementation with the project's structural evolution.",
			"SHA": "4fe4f36573ded1bcb2595c40207e30b8d36eab3b"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-03T08:19:50Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1482,
				5
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Decompose Enhanced IPC modules and enforce PascalCase struct qualification\n\nRemove the monolithic type definitions previously embedded directly in `Source/IPC/Enhanced/ConnectionPool.rs`, `MessageCompressor.rs`, `PerformanceDashboard.rs`, and `SecureMessageChannel.rs`. This refactor prepares the `IPC::Enhanced` layer for a fine-grained modular structure where specific traits and DTOs (e.g., `PoolConfig`, `Compressor::Struct`) reside in dedicated sub-files, aligning with the project's strict PascalCase naming conventions.\n\nUpdate `Source/IPC/Enhanced/mod.rs` to reference these types using explicit qualification (e.g., `ConnectionPool::Pool::Struct` instead of `ConnectionPool::ConnectionPool`). This resolves symbol shadowing issues caused by module-name/type-name collisions and adheres to the architectural shift towards explicit namespace resolution seen in recent command handler refactorings.\n\nThis change cleans up the current implementation state, allowing the `EnhancedIPCManager` to correctly instantiate its internal components (`Compressor`, `Pool`, `Channel`, `Dashboard`) once the corresponding sub-modules are migrated to their own files.",
			"SHA": "51dd389c370787f41e36f29c4e245375e6d4f620"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-03T08:19:45Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1486,
				5
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Modularize DNS and TLS command modules into sub-files\n\nSplit the monolithic `DnsCommands.rs` and `TlsCommands.rs` files into a directory structure of individual sub-modules, adhering to the project's strict PascalCase naming conventions. Each command handler, DTO, and utility now resides in its own file (e.g., `DnsServerInfo`, `ZoneInfo`, `tls_check_cert_status`), reducing file size and improving maintainability.\n\nConcurrently, updated `LoggingPlugin.rs` to align helper method calls with the new `::Fn()` explicit qualification pattern and refined `PostHogPlugin.rs` documentation to include the new `CaptureHandler` and `HydrateRuntimeEnvironment` modules. Removed extensive inline documentation in favor of concise module-level comments, as the new file structure provides natural separation of concerns.\n\nThis refactoring prepares the codebase for easier registration in `Entry.rs` and aligns with the architectural shift towards fine-grained modularity within the `Binary/Build` layer.",
			"SHA": "3ab7ccaa338e67a0aeb0e24a528cb57b4112782a"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-03T08:19:29Z",
